e": 0.9}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR was created, but the response shows no reviewers attached. I'll explicitly request alex's review on PR 101.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01BGbzak5C9ppMVWRViDwEyn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "reviewers": ["alex"], "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "request_review", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed and PR #101 is open against main with alex requested as reviewer.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 requires `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. For example, 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding` (commit `08d3cd5986`), I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101. The open call returned no reviewers, so I sent a separate review request to alex, which went through.\n\nNothing was merged. Merging into main needs code-owner approval under policy. The PR description notes that any caller relying on half-up behavior at exact midpoints will now get different results, so it's worth checking callers before this ships.", "type": "text"}]}]}